# The deployment scripts run on Linux. A CRLF line ending in a shell script
# makes the kernel look for an interpreter named "bash\r", which fails as
# `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` — a confusing error for
# a file that looks perfectly fine in an editor. Pin these to LF so it cannot
# happen no matter what a contributor's core.autocrlf is set to.
*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.dockerignore text eol=lf
Caddyfile     text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf

# Let git decide for everything else.
* text=auto
